  id: Right_Aortic_Arch3
  partName: Right Aortic Arch
  descriptionChunks:
  - 'The right aortic arch represents an anatomical variant in which the aorta curves
    to the right rather than the left. In dogs, a persistent right aortic arch can
    form a vascular ring around the esophagus and trachea, potentially causing compression
    and obstruction. '
  - This structure, though typically a developmental variant, plays a role in vascular
    anatomy and blood distribution. Understanding its presence is important for diagnosing
    congenital cardiovascular conditions that may affect respiration and digestion
    in affected animals.
